# Gateway endpoints, in priority order. The app probes both at launch and uses
# whichever answers first, re-probing when a request fails — so you can move
# from the desk (USB) to mobile data without editing anything here.
#
# See src/lib/api/endpoint.ts.

# Tried FIRST. The Cloudflare tunnel — reachable from anywhere, which is what
# lets the app work off your machine's network.
#
# A quick tunnel prints a new random hostname every time it starts, so paste
# the current one here (scripts/tunnel.sh writes it to infra/tunnel-url.txt).
# With a named tunnel on a domain you own the hostname is stable and you set
# this once. Leave unset to use localhost only.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_TUNNEL_URL=https://your-tunnel.trycloudflare.com

# Fallback, used when the tunnel is down or unset.
#   - over USB:   adb reverse tcp:8080 tcp:8080, then localhost works
#   - over Wi-Fi: your machine's LAN IP, e.g. http://192.168.1.10:8080
#     (localhost on a phone means the phone itself, not your laptop)
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
